Implement a major gameplay update introducing a new elite stealth-assassin mech unit, focused heavily on cinematic takedowns, high-speed teleportation, interactive timing-based combat, and exceptionally polished procedural animations.

The game is heavily inspired by **86: Eighty-Six**, so the new unit must fit the existing futuristic military atmosphere, mechanical designs, squad combat systems, and enemy AI.

**THE MAIN FOCUS OF THIS UPDATE IS ANIMATION QUALITY.**

Do not treat the animations as secondary visual additions. The takedowns, teleportation, combat interactions, enemy reactions, camera movements, and first-person sequences must be among the most polished features in the game.

Avoid basic animations, stiff movements, robotic-looking transitions, or repetitive sequences. Make the entire experience feel like an intense cinematic mech assassination system.

Inspect the existing unit framework, animation controller, camera system, damage system, enemy AI, squad AI, and combat mechanics before implementation. Reuse existing systems wherever possible.

