**6. APPLY THE SAME MINIGAME TO THE PLAYER'S SQUADMATES**

The new takedown system must also work when friendly AI squadmates perform assassinations.

When a squadmate using the stealth-assassin unit initiates a takedown, the same interactive minigame should be used where appropriate.

However, friendly AI must not be forced to wait for the player to manually complete every minigame.

Implement an AI resolution system.

**AI minigame resolution:**

When a friendly squadmate performs the timing minigame, give it a flat 50% chance of successfully beating the minigame.

This must be a genuine 50% success probability, not a variable chance secretly modified by difficulty, unit health, enemy type, or other factors.

The result should be determined independently for each eligible minigame.

- 50% chance: AI successfully beats the minigame.
- 50% chance: AI fails the minigame.

The outcome should determine whether the squadmate successfully completes the takedown or the enemy resists and potentially retaliates.

Even though the result is automatically calculated for AI, the same minigame interface and animation sequence should remain visually present where appropriate.

Do not display fake player inputs or pretend the AI is pressing buttons.

The minigame should resolve naturally through the AI system.

Make sure multiple squadmates performing separate takedowns do not interfere with one another's minigame resolution.

If the enemy breaks free, the squadmate should transition back into normal combat AI.

